---
import cli from '../../../../packages/cli/package.json'
import Heading from '../components/Heading.astro'
import Next from '../components/Next.astro'
import Replay from '../components/Replay'
import Snippet from '../components/Snippet.astro'
import Terminal from '../components/Terminal'
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
import { capture } from '../lib/captures'
---

<Page
  page="monitor"
  title="Monitor"
  description="Compile the same tests into one file that runs with just node, and run it on a schedule in production."
>
  <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 24px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">04 · Monitor</span>
      <h1 class="display">One file. Just node.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        <code>specbook bundle</code> compiles your requests and flows, their dependencies and the runner into a
        single <code>.mjs</code> file. Run it on any machine with node, on a schedule in production. It needs no
        install and no spec, and it holds no secrets.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" style="padding-top: 8px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Heading>Build one file</Heading>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Compile the tests you want to watch. The file holds your requests and flows and the runner, and a{' '}
          <code>.sha256</code> file beside it lets your pipeline verify the download.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Snippet file="snippets/install.sh" region="monitor" title={false} />

      <Heading>Run it anywhere</Heading>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Node is all the machine needs. This recording runs the file against a staging address.</p>
      </div>
      <Replay client:visible capture={capture('bundle-run')} />

      <Heading>Know when it breaks</Heading>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This is the same run in your browser. Choose what the demo API does, then press Run. When the API is
          down every request errors and the run exits 1, which is what pages someone.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Terminal client:visible tag="monitor" chaos={['calm', 'down', 'flaky', 'missing']} version={cli.version} />
      <Replay client:visible capture={capture('test-down')} />

      <Heading>Keep production safe</Heading>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          By default a run sends everything, so you can test flows that create and delete against a lower
          environment. Against production, pass <strong><code>--safe</code></strong>. Any request that is not a
          GET, HEAD or OPTIONS (or a GraphQL query) is refused before it is sent, so a monitor cannot change
          production data. Mark a POST that only reads with <code>safe: true</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <code>--retries 1</code> runs a failed flow once more, and one that then passes is reported as flaky and
          exits 0. <code>--timeout</code> limits each request. The report separates failed from errored, so an API
          that is down reads differently from one that answered wrongly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Heading>Run it on a schedule</Heading>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>A scheduled workflow downloads the file, runs it and fails when a flow does.</p>
      </div>
      <Snippet file="snippets/monitor-workflow.yml" region="workflow" title="monitor.yml" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap"><Next page="monitor" /></div>
</Page>

